# Workflow

## Commits

Conventional Commits. Subject under 72 chars, imperative, no trailing period.

```
feat(core): weight letter bag by frequency table
fix(core): reshuffle discard when draw pile empties mid-hand
test(core): cover scoring multipliers for 7-letter words
```

Describe what changed, not where the work came from. `fix PR13 review findings`
is a bad subject; `scope build strictness to Core` is a good one.

Footer: `Closes #42`.

## Branches

`feat/42-letter-bag-draw`, `fix/57-shuffle-off-by-one`, `chore/12-bump-godot`.
The issue number is part of the name. One issue, one branch, one PR.

Branches live hours to days. Older than four days means the issue was too big
and should have been split.

## Pull requests

`main` is protected. Never commit to it directly, never suggest doing so.

Fill in `.github/pull_request_template.md` completely, including the review
brief that tells a reviewer where to attack. CI must be green before review.
Squash merge, then delete the branch.

## Before committing

Run `dotnet format WordRoguelike.Core.sln` — CI fails on unformatted code.

## Decisions

Non-reversible choices go in `docs/adr/` using `docs/adr/template.md`. Never
delete an ADR; supersede it and mark the old one's status.
